{
  "dom_id": "step-q334129",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)+4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-4,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[2,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-2,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Which of the following could represent the phase portrait of the system?\n\n*Hint: Here, the dotted line represents the equilibrium solutions.*",
  "worked_solution": "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nLet's now sketch the phase portrait.\n\n- First, notice that ${x}_{E}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ are the equilibrium solutions of the system since ${x}_{E}^{′}(t)=0.$ These solutions form the line with the equation $y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ in the phase space, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274360/assets/9aa57af0c1950be0b52f9a4c5d9abe8dd86fc82ef874f09beed6cbb1e924f31b.png)\n\n- Now, the line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n$y=-\\frac{1}{2}x$\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line. Since ${e}^{-4t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274360/assets/3296a5305332592542386ac439b911fec19a6ecfb2d82bf5aec440177c30d47f.png)\n\nAll other non-equilibrium solutions are parallel to the vector ${v}_{2}.$ So, the phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14274360/assets/475a2dc2e5e9301afeb1e9d123568912a98469514c4385f765ecb41f29c8c430.png)",
